  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscComm 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a community meeting, a research team discusses a new lab-based
    cancer research project. You share this information with patients and physicians
    in your community and bring their questions back to the team. \r\n\r\n<b>Community
    advocates can help build trust and transparency between the research team and
    the patient community, even in the earliest stage of clinical research.</b>\r\n\nIs
    this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Involving community advocates early helps researchers stay connected
    to patient needs and ensures the community understands why and how the research
    is happening. This early engagement builds trust and prepares the way for future
    studies. By sharing their perspectives and asking questions, community advocates
    help make the research process more transparent and meaningful for cancer patients
    and families.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
